# Brand colors

Use only this palette. Map to CSS variables / Shadcn theme tokens rather than scattering one-off hex values.

| Hex | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `#ffc527` | Primary buttons; headings sitting on dark backgrounds |
| `#222222` | Dark surfaces (footer and similar); heading text on light backgrounds |
| `#434343` | Paragraph / body text on light backgrounds |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — random accent, light heading on dark footer
<button className="bg-blue-600">Get a quote</button>
<footer className="bg-black text-white">
  <h2 className="text-white">Our services</h2>
  <p className="text-white/80">We renovate villas and flats.</p>
</footer>

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="bg-[#ffc527] text-[#222222]">Get a quote</button>
<footer className="bg-[#222222]">
  <h2 className="text-[#ffc527]">Our services</h2>
  <p className="text-white/80">We renovate villas and flats.</p>
</footer>
```

Prefer theme tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-foreground`) once they are wired to these hex values. Until then, use the hexes above.

# Fonts

Use **two typefaces** (heading vs body/UI). Do not ship the finished site on a single family. Family names are TBD — do not invent them. Starter Geist is a placeholder until named.
